      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Full text of Margaret M. Curtis' memoir of the struggle for passage of the Equal Rights Amendment in Georgia. The book was \"published on the occasion of the Fifteenth Anniversary of the Georgia Women's Movement Project by the Georgia State Unversity Library's Women's Collection.\" The book was printed in a paper edition of 150 copies that were presented to donors to the Women's Collection at the 2010 Diane L. Fowlkes Spring Event, \"Passing the Torch at the Water's Edge\" (April 19). Publication was supported by Our Mother's Fund established by Margaret Miller Curtis and Dorothy Gibson-Ferrey, and edited by Morna Gerrard, William Hardesty, and Stephen Zietz."
